+### Compound Durations
+
+Use `parseCompound` to sum several parts into one value. Parts can be separated by spaces, commas, and/or "and". It throws a `TypeError` if any part is invalid.
+
+```ts
+import { parseCompound } from 'ms';
+
+parseCompound('1h 30m'); // 5400000
+parseCompound('1h, 30m'); // 5400000
+parseCompound('2 days and 4 hours'); // 187200000
+```
+
 ### Enhanced Type Safety
 
 If you want strict type checking for the input value, you can use `parseStrict`.
